  "bindingRules": [
    "Live Nodal HVL is the richer default execution capability.",
    "Portable Nodal HVL is an explicit structured subset of the same public language.",
    "Projection eligibility is a capability set, not one universal Boolean.",
    "Verilog-TB and UVM are independent sibling profiles and neither inherits from the other.",
    "A live test may call captured components only when all required operations have qualified live implementations.",
    "A portable component may call Portable Core operations, compatible profile operations, deterministic precomputable helpers or declared companion-runtime services.",
    "Projection rejection never invalidates otherwise-supported live execution; generated-only extensions do not imply live eligibility.",
    "Generated backend limitations must never remove or weaken a live API operation.",
    "A package may support Verilog-TB, UVM, both or neither.",
    "Diagnostics identify the first incompatible operation, source location, required capability and legal modes."
